'''urocyst''' (ū′rọ̄-sist), ''n.'' [< NL. ''urocystis'', < Gr. οὖρον, urine, + κύστις, bladder: see ''cyst''.] The permanently pervious part of the cavity of the allantois of a mammal, for the reception and detention of urine; the urinary bladder; the cystic vesicle.

'''urocystic''' (ū-rọ̄-sis′tik), ''a.'' [< ''urocyst'' + ''-ic''.] Of or pertaining to the urinary bladder; cystic; vesical.

